mod_research_name.ALTERNATIVEVISFILTER=Alternative Filter
mod_research_text.ALTERNATIVEVISFILTER=Too lazy for finding Silverwood ?
mod_research_page.ALTERNATIVEVISFILTER.1=You explored miles and miles of land, without ever finding that legendary white tree ... Or maybe you didn't ? <LINE> In your sleepless night out there in the wild, you actually thought of an insane way of faking a replicate of a Silverwood plank by using a composition of different shiny metals <BR> Faking thaumaturgy basic elements is almost impossible, so you will need a crazy amount of Ordo to sharpen any bad lines on that fake birch plank !
#
mod_research_name.ALTERNATIVELEATHER=Alternative Leather
mod_research_text.ALTERNATIVELEATHER=Let's skin those zombies
mod_research_page.ALTERNATIVELEATHER.1=After miles and miles of exploration, it seems that all cows were abducted somewhere else nowhere to be found ... Or maybe you were too lazy for searching around ? <BR> Whatever, in your wildest dreams, you thought of a preparation to purify that nasty pile of zombie rotten flesh into tanned leather. <LINE> The process is not efficient at all, and only outputs a few pieces of leather ... <BR> This process was so nasty, you promised yourself to never ever do it again !
#
mod_research_name.ALTERNATIVESILVERWOOD=Title
mod_research_text.ALTERNATIVESILVERWOOD=Subtitle
mod_research_page.ALTERNATIVESILVERWOOD.1=Something is off... The book tells you about a shimmering pale magical tree and yet you cannot find it anywhere in this damned world.<BR>Is this some kind of a joke?        - You ask yourself.<BR>And then suddenly something interesting happens in your entries, a desperate craft shows up, out of thin air! It feels like the book is yelling to you "You will have it just this time!"<BR>Either in desperation or just for a freebie, it seems like you have this one chance to bring this valuable sapling to your hands, do not think you will have another try!
#
mod_research_name.FLINTANDSTEEL=Flint and Steel
mod_research_text.FLINTANDSTEEL=We're on fire tonight !
mod_research_page.FLINTANDSTEEL.1=By hitting metal and flint together, you're able to generate some sparks ! <LINE> However, those sparks alone are too weak to even do anything ... But if you add a touch of thaumium, a condensate of fire and some Ignis vis ; you're able to make a tool that is capable to set a whole block on fire !
#
mod_research_name.VANILLAFURNACE=Stone Furnace
mod_research_text.VANILLAFURNACE=It burns !
mod_research_page.VANILLAFURNACE.1=After some struggles on your first steps through this world, you finally discover how to smelt items like your ancestors did.<LINE>You will need the sufficient amount of vis in your wand, then sneak and hit the coal block with it to transform the construct to a stone furnace !
#
mod_research_name.CAMPFIRE=Wooden Campfire
mod_research_text.CAMPFIRE=Let starvation behind
mod_research_page.CAMPFIRE.1=A basic caveman campfire shouldn't be too hard to make ... right ? <LINE> Any kind of vanilla wood logs and slabs can be used to process to turn this construct into an actual campfire ! <BR> Sneaking and right clicking the black carpet with your wand will trigger and magically turn the structure into a campfire.
mod_research_page.CAMPFIRE.3=You can lit it on fire by using certain items, or by using a bit of Ignis from your wand ! The campfire will die by itself after a few minutes. <LINE> While it is burning, you can cook up to four raw items - they will take around 20 to 30 seconds before they become eatable ! <BR> The campfire cannot be harvested, destroying it will only drop some charcoal.
#
mod_research_name.CAMPFIRE_SOUL=Soul Campfire
mod_research_text.CAMPFIRE_SOUL=Rising from the ashes
mod_research_page.CAMPFIRE_SOUL.1=After surviving some nights inside a hole with the fear of dying, you start thinking of ways to bring your soul back to this realm, at an exact location, in case of the inevitable death happening.<BR>Your previous life experiences tell you to make a bed, but the recipe you remember is not available anymore.<BR>There must be a thaumaturgical way of doing that!<BR>And that's when a genius idea hits you: using the aspect of soul paired with a gravestone, you can make a magical respawn point!
mod_research_page.CAMPFIRE_SOUL.3=This campfire is special and will burn as long as your soul is "alive".<BR>To link your soul to it, the campfire must be lit and then you need to sneak and right click the campfire with your bare hands. Once done, if you happen to die, you'll respawn right next to it and its blue flames will extinguish.<LINE>You can lit the soul campfire again with a wand, the same way as you did on the regular one ; But you need more aspects stored for this, and only the wand will be able to lit this campfire, nothing else.
mod_research_page.CAMPFIRE_SOUL.6=Here's the recipe for the gravestone to complete your research. Once you've built the whole structure, make sure your wand got the required vis then sneak and right click the gravestone with it ; shall an unlit soul campfire appear magically !<LINE>Remember, this campfire is as fragile as the mundane one, so a careful thaumaturge would not treat such special flames irresponsibly.
#
